      "text": "Since \\(\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2\\), we can use the property of determinants that states \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^n) = (\\det \\mathbf{M})^n\\) for any positive integer \\(n\\).\n\nIn this problem, we are asked to find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\). Using the property mentioned above, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det \\mathbf{M})^4\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2\\), we substitute this value into the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2)^4\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\((-2)^4\\):\n\n\\[\n(-2)^4 = (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) = 16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
