      "text": "Given that $\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2$, we aim to find $\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)$.\n\nUsing the property of determinants, we know that for any invertible matrix $\\mathbf{A}$ and integer $n$:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{A}^n) = (\\det \\mathbf{A})^n\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $\\mathbf{M}$ is invertible (since $\\det \\mathbf{M} \\neq 0$), so $\\mathbf{M}^4$ is also invertible. Applying the property, we get:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det \\mathbf{M})^4\n\\]\n\nSubstituting $\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2$, we have:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2)^4\n\\]\n\nCalculating the power:\n\\[\n(-2)^4 = 16\n\\]\n\nThus, the determinant of $\\mathbf{M}^4$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
